// travel as themselves (narrow integers widened to 32 bits), structs of up
// to 16 bytes as one INTEGER or SSE scalar per eightbyte, and larger structs
// in memory: copied onto the stack as arguments, through a hidden pointer as
// results. Several results are returned as a struct of the results in order.
// The backend's ssa.ABIC mode then places the scalars, with CallInfo.OnStack
// (ssa.Func.ParamOnStack for export wrappers) forcing a struct to the stack
// when its eightbytes do not all fit in the registers left.
